.TH NYANCAT 1 "July, 2026"
.SH NAME
nyancat \- terminal-based Pop Tart Cat animation (Rust Edition)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nyancat [ \-iItnsebTVh ] [\-d ms] [\-f frames] [\-r row] [\-R row] [\-c col] [\-C col] [\-W width] [\-H height]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nyancat
is a high-performance, color, ANSI-text program written in Rust that renders a loop of the
classic Nyan Cat animation.
.PP
nyancat makes use of various ANSI escape sequences to render color, and supports 
24-bit TrueColor rendering for high-definition displays.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-i, \-\-intro
Show introduction / about information on startup.
.TP
.B \-I, \-\-skip\-intro
Skip the introduction in telnet mode.
.TP
.B \-t, \-\-telnet
Enable telnet protocol negotiation on standard input and standard output.
This option does not open a listening socket.
.TP
.B \-T, \-\-truecolor
Enable 24-bit TrueColor mode (high-definition rendering).
.TP
.B \-n, \-\-no\-counter
Do not display the timer.
.TP
.B \-s, \-\-no\-title
Do not set the titlebar text.
.TP
.B \-e, \-\-no\-clear
Do not clear the display between frames.
.TP
.B \-b, \-\-benchmark
Run in benchmark mode (0ms delay). Warning: high CPU and bandwidth usage.
When combined with
.B \-\-frames,
prints a key-value benchmark report to stderr after the terminal is restored.
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-delay
Delay image rendering by anywhere between 10ms and 1000ms.
.br
The program exits with an error if the amount is out of range.
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-frames
Display the requested positive number of frames, then quit.
.TP
.B \-r, \-\-min\-rows
Crop the animation from the top.
.br
Accepted range: \-10000 to 10000.
.TP
.B \-R, \-\-max\-rows
Crop the animation from the bottom.
.br
Accepted range: \-10000 to 10000.
.TP
.B \-c, \-\-min\-cols
Crop the animation from the left.
.br
Accepted range: \-10000 to 10000.
.TP
.B \-C, \-\-max\-cols
Crop the animation from the right.
.br
Accepted range: \-10000 to 10000.
.TP
.B \-W, \-\-width
Crop the animation to the given width.
.br
Accepted range: 1 to 10000.
.TP
.B \-H, \-\-height
Crop the animation to the given height.
.br
Accepted range: 1 to 10000.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help message and exit.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Show version information and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set to a non-empty value, render in monochrome ASCII and omit styling from help and diagnostics (see https://no\-color.org). Render-mode selection is ignored in telnet mode, where color is the connecting client's concern.
.SH TELNET DEPLOYMENT
.PP
Network access requires a socket activation or inetd-style service.
The included systemd socket unit listens on TCP port 23 on all interfaces by default,
and telnet traffic is unencrypted. Before enabling it, bind
.B ListenStream
to a trusted interface, such as 127.0.0.1:23, or restrict TCP port 23 with a firewall.
